Generate an authorized_keys line with apps/agent/install_forced_command.py.
Use a dedicated Ed25519 key generated on the service server. Transfer only its public key.
Install the emitted line under the account that owns /etc/jasmin encrypted credentials
(initial implementation: root). Preserve existing authorized_keys entries and set mode 0600.
The restrict/from/command options apply to this dedicated key only. Other existing keys
are not made restricted by this installation. Do not install the same dedicated key
anywhere without the restrictive options. The runner permits only jasmin-job-v1.
The Python interpreter, repository, parent directories and config directory must be
root-owned and not writable by other users. The server's known_hosts must be verified
out of band and stored with mode 0600. Never disable host key checking.
The source IP and interface must match an operator-managed, verified management route.
The Cloudflare application Tunnel does not supply this SSH management path.
This helper does not create users, change sshd_config or restart SSH.
